  "title": "Radical tumor resection",
  "description": "Radical tumor resection is extensive surgical removal of a malignant tumor along with surrounding tissue and potentially lymph nodes to ensure complete cancer removal. Your surgeon removes the tumor with substantial margins and may remove involved regional lymph nodes. This aggressive approach is used for tumors with higher recurrence risk or aggressive behavior. The procedure may leave a larger scar but provides the best chance of complete cancer removal. Pathology examination confirms complete removal.",
